# Related work

Pang, J. C., Aquino, K. M., Oldehinkel, M., Robinson, P. A.,
Fulcher, B. D., Breakspear, M., and Fornito, A. (2023).
"Geometric constraints on human brain function."
Nature 618(7965): 566–574.
DOI: https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06098-1
Article URL: https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-023-06098-1
Local copy: ./article/s41586-023-06098-1.pdf (CC BY 4.0, see paper)

This paper demonstrates that resting and task-evoked cortical activity
in human fMRI is well described by Laplace–Beltrami eigenmodes of the
brain's geometry — i.e., resonant modes of a Laplacian on a biological
substrate — rather than by modes of connectivity graphs. It is the
closest published analogue of GRM applied to physiology and is the
intellectual context for this repository's spectral / resonance choice.
The GRM-TCM benchmark does NOT claim equivalence with the brain-imaging
result; it uses the same family of methods on a different (synthetic,
longitudinal, integrative-physiology) substrate.

